   "id": 666511,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the output?\n<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">numbers = [1, 2, 2, 6]\nfor i in numbers:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;if i &gt;= 5:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print(\"Not all numbers are less than 5.\")\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;break\n&nbsp;&nbsp;else:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print(i)\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;continue\nelse:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;print(\"all numbers are less than 5.\")</pre>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1328586,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">1\n2\n2\n6\nNot all numbers are less than 5.\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "When <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">i = 6</code>, the <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">if</code> condition evaluates as true and \"Not all numbers are less than 5.\" is printed. Yet, the integer value 6 is not printed."
    },
    {
     "id": 1328587,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">1\n2\n2\nNot all numbers are less than 5.\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "The loop iterates over all integer values in the list. If a value is less than <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">5</code>, the value will be printed, and if the value is greater than <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">5</code>, the code prints \"<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">Not all numbers are less than 5.</code>\" and the code's execution terminates."
    },
    {
     "id": 1328588,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">1\n2\n2\n6\nall numbers are less than 5.\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "When <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">i = 6</code>, the<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\"> if</code> condition evaluates as true and \"Not all numbers are less than 5.\" is printed. Does the loop's execution terminate at this point?"
    }
   ],
